<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolt</p><h1 class="enc-title">The Fronde</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1648">1648</a>–<a href="/years/1653">1653</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Fronde</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Fronde was a series of revolts in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> between 1648 and 1653 during the minority of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xiv">Louis XIV</a>. It began with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parlement-of-paris">Parlement of Paris</a> resisting new taxes imposed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jules-mazarin">Cardinal Mazarin</a> and grew into a rebellion of great nobles led by princes such as Condé. The royal family twice fled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a>, but the revolts failed, and memories of the disorder encouraged Louis XIV's later absolutism.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/the-fronde.jpg" alt="The Fronde" width="320" height="259" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Combat_de_deux_cavaliers_lors_de_la_Fronde,_faubourg_Saint-Antoine,_sous_les_murs_de_la_Bastille.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
